/-!
# Real klt boundaries on a fixed support: openness and rational klt polytopes

Let `X` be a normal `ℚ`-factorial quasi-projective variety over an algebraically closed field of
characteristic zero and `p : ι → PrimeDivisor X` a finite family of prime divisors. A coefficient
vector `x ∈ ℝ^ι` gives the real divisor `∑ᵢ xᵢ pᵢ`. The vectors in the nonnegative cone for which
this divisor is a klt boundary form a relatively open subset of the cone, and so do those for which
it is a real terminal boundary. Consequently, on a projective such variety a real klt boundary `Δ`
lies in the relative interior of a rational polytope, spanning the smallest rational affine
subspace through `Δ`, whose rational vertices give klt pairs.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.eventually_isRealKltPair_and_isRealTerminalPair`: klt and real terminal
  boundaries on a fixed support are relatively open in the nonnegative cone.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_rationalPolytope_isKltPair_of_isRealKltPair`: a rational klt polytope
  through a real klt boundary.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_isLogDiscrepancy_add_sum`: adding real multiples of Cartier divisors to
  the boundary moves every log discrepancy affinely.
* `MMP.Fourfold.convex_setOf_lt_isLogDiscrepancy_add`,
  `MMP.Fourfold.convex_setOf_lt_isLogDiscrepancy`: klt regions along Cartier directions, and in a
  fixed coefficient space, are convex.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_rat_convexHull_mem_nhds`: every neighbourhood of `x ∈ ℝ^ι` contains
  rational points whose convex hull is a neighbourhood of `x`.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_resolution_data`: on a log resolution of the support, the log
  discrepancies are affine in the coefficients, with rational klt, terminal and plt criteria.
* `MMP.Fourfold.isKltPair_of_isRealKltPair`: an effective `ℚ`-divisor that is a real klt
  boundary on a `ℚ`-factorial variety gives a klt pair.

## Implementation notes

Each result's auxiliary lemmas live in a namespace `Proof_<tag>` named after its label,
opened only for that result. Openness is proved on a log resolution of the support of `∑ pᵢ`
(`MMP.Mori.exists_isLogResolution`): the log discrepancies of the components of its snc divisor,
and of the blow-ups of their pairwise intersections, are affine functions of the coefficient
vector, and the klt and terminal conditions for rational vectors follow from strict inequalities
on them; real vectors near `x` are convex combinations of rational ones. Openness relative to the
nonnegative cone is stated in its filter form `∀ᶠ y in 𝓝[Set.Ici 0] x`. The rational polytope is
the convex hull of a finite set of rational vectors, the corners of a rational parallelotope from
`MMP.Fourfold.rational_hull_neighborhood` taken inside the klt neighbourhood.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori], 2.31, 2.34
-/

@[expose] public section

